+# Summary: range matching (`depres/ranges.py`)
+
+## What changed
+- `depres/ranges.py`: implemented `satisfies(version, range_)` and `max_satisfying(versions, range_)` per `docs/RANGES.md`.
+  - Parses `||` unions, whitespace-separated comparator sets, and the empty set (matches all).
+  - Supports primitive comparators (`< <= > >= =`, bare = exact), operator-space-version (`>= 1.2.3`), X-ranges (`x X *`), partial versions with operators, hyphen ranges, tilde, and caret.
+  - Applies the prerelease rule: a prerelease version matches a set only if some comparator in that set names the same release with a prerelease.
+  - Invalid ranges and invalid versions raise `ValueError`. `max_satisfying` returns the item as given, or `None`.
+- `tests/test_ranges_contract.py` (new): 23 tests covering the tables and rules in `docs/RANGES.md`. No existing test was edited or deleted.
+
+## Verification
+- `python -m unittest -v` (run from the project root): 23 tests, all OK. This includes the 8 tests in `tests/test_ranges.py`, which previously all errored.
+- Changed files: `depres/ranges.py`, `tests/test_ranges_contract.py`, `SUMMARY.md`.
+
+## Not verified / open points
+- I did not compare against a reference npm/semver implementation. Behavior follows the written spec and my reading of it.
+- Hyphen ranges must be the whole comparator set (`A - B`). Mixing in extra comparators (e.g. `1.2 - 2 <3`) raises `ValueError`. The spec does not say what should happen there, so I chose to reject it.
+- `max_satisfying` returns the first item when two candidates compare equal (e.g. `1.0.0` and `1.0.0+build`).
+- Not run: linters or type checkers. The repo has no config for them that I checked.
